<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Cape Verde</h1><p class="st-meta">1975 CE – present · capital Praia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An archipelago republic off West Africa, independent from Portugal in 1975, a multi-party democracy since the early 1990s.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-cape-verde">Portuguese Cape Verde</a> became an overseas province in 1951. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paigc">PAIGC</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amilcar-cabral">Amílcar Cabral</a> in 1956, took up arms in Portuguese Guinea, and after the April 1974 revolution in Portugal it became an active movement in Cape Verde. The islands received their instruments of independence on 5 July 1975.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Independence followed the movement led by Cabral until his assassination in 1973, and the state was governed under a constitution adopted in 1980 and revised in 1992, 1995 and 1999. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristides">Aristides</a> Pereira, who took over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paigc">PAIGC</a> leadership after the assassination of Cabral, became the first president. Since the early 1990s it has been a multi-party representative democracy, in which the two main parties are PAICV and MpD. The economy has few natural resources and is mostly service-oriented, with a growing focus on tourism and foreign investment.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Cape Verde is a unitary semi-presidential republic. The president is elected by popular vote for five years, and the prime minister is nominated by the National Assembly. The country adopted its own national anthem in 1996, and on 2 February 2024 it became the third African country to be free of malaria.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cape-verde.jpg" alt="Cape Verde" width="330" height="195"><figcaption>Image: Original: Pedro Gregório Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cape_Verde_(10-17).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1975 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt>